---
Semantic grep that stays local

Usage: ig [OPTIONS] [QUERY] [PATH] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  context   Build one task-aware, token-budgeted context bundle
  agent     Install and verify ivygrep for coding agents
  hardware  Detect hardware, installed backend, and best available build
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [QUERY]  Natural-language question, keyword, identifier, or exact search text
  [PATH]   Workspace, subdirectory, or file to search. Defaults to current directory

Options:
      --add [<PATH>]          Index PATH and register it for incremental updates. Defaults to current directory
      --rm [<PATH>]           Remove PATH's saved index. Defaults to current directory
      --status                Show tracked workspaces, index health, vector coverage, and disk usage
      --doctor                Diagnose index, daemon, watcher, and model health for PATH
      --fix                   Repair a broken or stale index (used with --doctor)
      --deep                  Perform full cross-store integrity scans (used with --doctor)
      --daemon                Run long-lived indexing, search, MCP, and web services
      --web                   Open the daemon-backed local web UI
      --host <HOST>           Host for --web. Non-loopback access requires the token in the printed URL [default: 127.0.0.1]
      --port <PORT>           Port for --web. Use 0 to let the OS choose a free port [default: 4747]
      --mcp                   Serve Model Context Protocol tools over stdio
      --wait-for-enhancement  Wait for requested vector enhancement and report worker failures
  -f, --force                 Rebuild workspace index from scratch when used with --add
      --interactive           Launch the interactive terminal UI [aliases: --ui]
  -l, --literal               Fast exact-match search backed by the index. Deterministic results, orders of magnitude faster than grep/rg for indexed repos
      --symbol                Find exact symbol definitions
      --refs                  Find exact symbol references
      --callers               Find functions or methods that call the named symbol
      --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON without ANSI styling
  -C, --context <LINES>       Lines before and after the focused match to include in each snippet. This changes output size, not retrieval ranking [default: 2]
      --type <TYPE_FILTER>    Filter by language name, extension, or alias (e.g. rust, rs, py, python, c++, bash, md)
      --all-indices           Search every tracked workspace instead of resolving one PATH
      --include <GLOBS>       Include only comma-separated path globs. May be repeated
      --exclude <GLOBS>       Exclude comma-separated path globs. May be repeated
  -n, --limit <FILES>         Retrieval breadth and maximum ranked result files, not a token, line, or confidence limit. Larger values search deeper and may improve recall
      --no-limit              Use maximum candidate budgets and return all surviving results. This can produce large, slower responses
      --no-watch              Index once without starting or registering a filesystem watcher
      --first-line-only       Return only the first non-empty preview line. Ranking is unchanged
      --file-name-only        Return only file paths. Without --limit, this also uses maximum candidate budgets; combine with --limit for a bounded path list
      --verbose               Include source-signal explanations and detailed progress diagnostics
      --skip-gitignore        Include files excluded by .gitignore and other standard ignore files
      --hash                  Use lightweight hash-based embeddings instead of the default neural model. Faster startup, no model download, lower quality
      --lexical-only          Use BM25/path/signature retrieval without vector search
  -h, --help                  Print help
  -V, --version               Print version

Examples:
  ig "where is authentication checked?"
  ig context "fix refresh-token races" --budget 8000
  ig agent install claude
  ig hardware
  ig --literal validate_token src/
  ig --symbol UserService
  ig --add . --wait-for-enhancement
  ig --status
  ig --web
